Question Two: Agent Frameworks and Implementation
a) Intelligent Agent Design: Forensic DNA Analysis
For identifying victims of the Shakahola tragedy, we design an agent focused on genomic
sequencing. Below is the PEAS and PAGE categorization.
PEAS Elements:
Performance Measure: Precision and recall of genetic matches, speed of report
generation, and reduction of misidentification errors.
Environment: Laboratory data clusters, Ministry of Health databases, forensic sample
archives, and hospital registries.
• 
• Actuators: Generation of victim identification reports, digital status displays, and
automated database updates for legal authorities.
Sensors: High-throughput DNA sequencers, biometric scanners, and data interfaces for
family reference samples.
PAGE Elements:
Percepts: Raw genomic sequence data, family lineage DNA strings, forensic metadata
from site recovery, and missing person records.
Actions: Comparing DNA markers, flagging high-confidence matches, identifying
lineage anomalies, and notifying investigative teams.
Goals: To achieve accurate and rapid identification of all remains, establish biological
lineage between victims and relatives, and facilitate forensic closure.
Environment: The computational and physical setting, including genomic sequence
repositories, laboratory infrastructures, and secure cloud databases.
b) Python Implementation: Reflex Vacuum Agent
class VacuumAgent:
def __init__(self):
self.state = {'A': 'Dirty', 'B': 'Dirty'}
self.location = 'A'
def sense_and_act(self):
while 'Dirty' in self.state.values():
 current_status = self.state[self.location]
if current_status == 'Dirty':
self.state[self.location] = 'Clean'
self.location = 'B' if self.location == 'A' else 'A'
print("System Report: Cleaning operations complete.")